Reason: \"Operator-authorized for this session and comment-remediation epic: bypass stale plan-review certification for prose-only remediation.\".","timestamp":1792719037093064525},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"At origin/main dcb35ce77fecb1d60e5ca00d2f875245a9dc820d, the pinned basis 0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e predates executable changes in owned paths, including test_bridge_programmatic.py and test_cli_argparse.py. The recorded immutable-base AST comparison cannot pass unchanged. No code was edited in this session; revalidate the scoped blocks and rebase the semantic oracle to current main before grouped remediation.","timestamp":1792719233626577303},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Currentization at origin/main cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a: all 14 declared facades files survive, but 9 have executable drift since historical audit 0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e. Description and 7 DD commands now compare current-parent to final AST/directives and use executable local-venv commands; the older SHA remains historical provenance. Scoped prose blocks must be re-anchored to current source before editing, especially fsck/module, MCP JS/module, and MCP list-read docs. This leaf remains active and is paired with the 6-path plan-review leaf in a grouped Gerrit change.","timestamp":1792780896186008423},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLAIM: plan-review gate bypassed by user approval — no plan-review attestation was verified. Reason: \"Operator-authorized for this session and comment-remediation epic: ordinary claim failed on a stale plan review after reanchoring 14 facades paths from historical 0033662 to current main cbc02f0; sign-review confirmed description drift. Comment-only remediation requires no new planning review.\".","timestamp":1792780977061799556},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLAIM: plan-review gate bypassed by user approval — no plan-review attestation was verified. Reason: \"User-authorized comment-remediation epic exception: ordinary reclaim failed missing certified plan review; sign-review confirmed the existing PASS is stale because the executable-scope plan description was updated.\".","timestamp":1792784631621270405},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Group24 candidate 22d5265db6a4e34ccfb6bd2003a0bd9d4d294e52 is committed with this ticket trailer, bot DCO, and Gerrit Change-Id. The 14 scoped facade paths contain 38 shorter reviewed prose blocks. A nonauthor independently passed all 38 block contracts, current-parent/final citations, protected directives, normalized executable AST, unlisted comments, and writing policy. Focused facade plus companion tests passed as part of the 990 passed/4 skipped Group24 run; scoped Ruff, hygiene, and diff checks passed. Full make verify and Gerrit review/CI remain pending before closure.","timestamp":1792786928365762455}],"created_at":1788571117803828988,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"041d3021-4d89-429e-8fa4-2e941f532f6d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"4dbe-2a31-0a05-4c31"},{"link_uuid":"6f39069b-d107-4ced-a9f2-c0b9a112f874","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e57f-85cd-7960-41b6"},{"link_uuid":"bb7144b2-3836-4ff8-8599-8aa5c1fe4759","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e556-f298-57ff-43b1"},{"link_uuid":"646d4a93-3b1e-4ca3-a9bd-9f17e6334942","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2c12-1de0-faf9-400b"},{"link_uuid":"7819bee5-9d8c-4dd3-90f2-32a08f8487e4","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1879-e02b-d804-4094"},{"link_uuid":"1516c49e-1c85-4c6b-80ee-8fdefbaca77e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8c07-0e28-6403-4964"},{"link_uuid":"835f43b3-d2c9-48f1-b877-c0a9ae6aeeee","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e88e-2add-9fe3-4622"},{"link_uuid":"4c992fc7-f412-4d5d-9b80-4b3df96f9350","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b2a1-8862-1d2b-4e7f"},{"link_uuid":"a18c2b54-6e02-40aa-979d-16671aab525a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"860d-d90b-a77a-4b5b"},{"link_uuid":"f382f0c0-b9b4-493a-9247-2453270c49dc","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f0c1-a346-d839-4393"},{"link_uuid":"50f5aa23-c126-4c0e-93f5-1296c50ad714","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"eacc-5d49-6eb8-4f46"},{"link_uuid":"b81db648-20fd-4daa-ac31-9a0c60aa5229","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b113-e82f-cfb8-49d6"},{"link_uuid":"a56cb291-fb4f-4439-b29f-ec354eab0c9b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"dcb8-fb28-c690-4f64"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nFourteen `tests/interfaces/facades` files contain audited prose that repeats behavior, preserves incident history, or narrates obvious setup. The original audit used `origin/main@0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`. Current executable scope and before citations use `origin/main@cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a`; 9 owned paths have intervening executable changes, so the historical tree is provenance rather than the AST oracle.\n\n## Approach\nCondense only comments and true leading docstrings in the named blocks. Preserve non-docstring runtime strings, assertions, executable behavior, and exact shebang/tool directives.\n\nFor every changed Python file, parse current-parent (`cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a`) and final text with `type_comments=True`; remove only leading docstrings from modules, classes, functions, and async functions; normalize `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; and require the remaining ASTs to match. Compare shebang and directive-bearing physical lines separately and byte-for-byte.\n\n## Scope\n- `test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py` module prose — retain persisted-attestation parity and deliberate no-sign behavior.\n- `test_bridge_programmatic.py` Jira soft-degradation section, missing-project parameter note, and the docstrings on `test_incomplete_jira_scope_yields_a_typed_verdict_not_a_crash` and `test_absent_credentials_surface_as_a_typed_error_naming_the_variables` — retain typed fail-closed errors, required inputs, and no-network setup.\n- `test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py` module and scoped test prose — retain store-touching auto-mount and help/no-store non-mutation.\n- `test_cli_argparse.py` module prose — retain routing, stream, and exit contracts.\n- `test_cli_js_safe_integers.py` module and `ns_ticket` docstrings — retain JS-safe wire encoding and deterministic inexact timestamps; do not edit `_HLC_INEXACT_BASE_NS` or its assignment.\n- `test_fsck_structured_326f.py` module and scoped test prose — retain completed structured results, true failures, and separate recovery output.\n- `test_mcp.py::test_readonly_empty_env_is_a_fault_not_a_disable` docstring — retain the empty-value fail-closed contract and stronger error oracle.\n- `test_mcp_http_transport.py` scoped shutdown prose — retain instrument-before-offload, stop-intake, drain-before-exit, and the short uvicorn backstop.\n- `test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py` module and scoped test prose — retain JS-safe encoding, schema allowance, and agreement between structured/content response halves.\n- `test_mcp_list_read_surface.py` module and scoped test prose — retain lean-field exclusions, wire-size accounting, hard refusal, and valid remedies.\n- `test_mcp_push_status.py` module prose — retain caller-visible delivery state because server stderr is unavailable.\n- `test_mcp_stateless_transport.py` scoped transport prose — retain stateless blue-green routing and why retirement cannot rescue old session IDs.\n- `test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py` module and scoped test prose — retain retryability parity and sidecar-loss recovery.\n- `test_verify_completion_facades.py` module prose — retain CLI/MCP scope, offline seam, exit/schema contract, and default gating.\n\nPreserve every existing `noqa`, `type: ignore`, `pragma`, shebang, and test assertion exactly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only comments, true leading docstrings, or adjacent blank lines in Scope; normalized AST equality and exact directive-line comparison both pass.\n- [ ] Each edited block is shorter and keeps its current non-obvious contract or rationale without moving repetition, history, or ornament elsewhere.\n- [ ] A reviewer who did not author the edits posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block: path/block, current-parent before citation, final-commit after citation (or DELETED plus neighbor), preserved contract/consumer, before/after words, semantic-preservation verdict, bloat-removal verdict, and reviewer session.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `semantic-preservation=PASS` and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing or failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] Focused tests, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded normalized AST/directive guard, `pytest tests/interfaces/facades`, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and `make verify`. The independent TSV is authoritative for prose quality.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py","reason":"Condense scoped comments/docstrings; preserve attestation parity."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic.py","reason":"Condense scoped comments/docstrings; preserve typed Jira degradation."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py","reason":"Condense scoped comments/docstrings; preserve mount-gate behavior."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py","reason":"Condense module prose; preserve CLI routing contracts."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py","reason":"Condense module/fixture docstrings; preserve JS-safe timestamp behavior."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_fsck_structured_326f.py","reason":"Condense scoped comments/docstrings; preserve FSCK result contracts."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py","reason":"Condense the readonly-empty contract docstring; preserve fail-closed behavior."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py","reason":"Condense scoped shutdown comments; preserve transport ordering."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py","reason":"Condense scoped comments/docstrings; preserve MCP JS-safe encoding."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_read_surface.py","reason":"Condense scoped comments/docstrings; preserve lean-read contracts."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_push_status.py","reason":"Condense module prose; preserve caller-visible delivery state."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_stateless_transport.py","reason":"Condense scoped comments; preserve stateless transport rationale."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py","reason":"Condense scoped comments/docstrings; preserve attestation recovery."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py","reason":"Condense module prose; preserve completion facade contracts."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","2d43-3c39-307e-4450"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2d43-3c39-307e-4450","parent_status_uuid":"54196227-3a97-4d20-bbf0-45781af25743","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"6a8e-7f5b-ea0b-485c","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/interfaces/facades","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import ast, subprocess, sys\nBASE=\"cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a\"\nclass StripDocstrings(ast.NodeTransformer):\n    def generic_visit(self, node):\n        node = super().generic_visit(node)\n        if isinstance(node, (ast.Module, ast.ClassDef, ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)):\n            if node.body and isinstance(node.body[0], ast.Expr) and isinstance(node.body[0].value, ast.Constant) and isinstance(node.body[0].value.value, str):\n                node.body = node.body[1:]\n        if isinstance(node, ast.TypeIgnore):\n            node.lineno = 0\n        return node\ndef normalized(raw):\n    return StripDocstrings().visit(ast.parse(raw, type_comments=True))\nfor path in sys.argv[1:]:\n    before = subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", f\"{BASE}:{path}\"], text=True)\n    after = subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", f\"HEAD:{path}\"], text=True)\n    if ast.dump(normalized(before), include_attributes=False) != ast.dump(normalized(after), include_attributes=False):\n        raise SystemExit(f\"normalized AST changed: {path}\")' tests/interfaces/facades/test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_fsck_structured_326f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_read_surface.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_push_status.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_stateless_transport.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py","dd_id":"semantic","dd_text":"All scoped Python files have exactly equal normalized ASTs against the current parent."},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import re, subprocess, sys\nBASE=\"cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a\"\nPATTERN=re.compile(r\"^#!|#\\s*(?:noqa\\b|type:\\s*ignore\\b|pragma:\\s*no cover\\b|fmt:|ruff:|pyright:|mypy:)\")\ndef lines(ref, path):\n    raw=subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", f\"{ref}:{path}\"], text=True)\n    return [line for line in raw.splitlines() if PATTERN.search(line)]\nfor path in sys.argv[1:]:\n    before=lines(BASE, path)\n    after=lines(\"HEAD\", path)\n    if before != after:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"directive/shebang lines changed: {path}\")' tests/interfaces/facades/test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_fsck_structured_326f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_read_surface.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_push_status.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_stateless_transport.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py","dd_id":"directives","dd_text":"Shebang and directive-bearing physical lines remain byte-identical in every scoped file."},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import subprocess, sys\nexpected=sorted(sys.argv[1:])\nactual=sorted(subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"HEAD^..HEAD\"], text=True).splitlines())\nif actual != expected:\n    raise SystemExit(f\"changed paths differ from file impact: actual={actual!r} expected={expected!r}\")' tests/interfaces/facades/test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_fsck_structured_326f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_read_surface.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_push_status.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_stateless_transport.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py","dd_id":"paths","dd_text":"The one-commit leaf diff changes exactly the recorded file-impact paths."},{"command":"git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD -- tests/interfaces/facades/test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_fsck_structured_326f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_read_surface.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_push_status.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_stateless_transport.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py","dd_id":"diff","dd_text":"The impacted paths contain no whitespace errors."},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/interfaces/facades","dd_id":"focused","dd_text":"The complete interfaces/facades suite passes."},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","dd_id":"hygiene","dd_text":"The deterministic comment-hygiene policy passes."},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify","dd_id":"full","dd_text":"The complete repository verification passes."}]},"source_event_uuids":["0dcb587e-6c3a-4fb6-9d66-97198a4ab6b5","e1c5c6fe-40c5-448c-bec0-e6dcd4868d9a","e2a8c950-7155-463b-b731-270347360cce","e74c45fb-5ce1-440f-b1fe-633ea539efe1","608e364b-e45d-43e8-963d-208a7be4bfab","64533ae2-6059-46c7-a7f7-1ebc15cac484","62cb92c4-95f0-43d6-bb7e-f8247b6fefdc","f88f6697-47bd-441c-a920-8ae951b0eade","0b590063-c15d-4a93-89d3-a81b78fe2409","54196227-3a97-4d20-bbf0-45781af25743","b8fc009e-dc2b-4398-995f-dd5674cf360d","0f22162a-54d4-46db-a498-065f2f883004"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792788908978592761,"uuid":"cdfb7171-16b7-4463-a7a6-5f13d7118133"}